  "response_text": "A system call is a specific way that the user asks for information or for something to be written by the OS. The system call acts as a bridge between the user and the kernel. The user requests that something should be done like reading or writing but the user could break something if they were able to access this directly. So instead the user preforms a System Call which is like a function call except it is given to the kernel which has privileged access and that preforms the action. This adds a layer of security to prevent the user from accessing something they shouldn\u2019t.\\n",
